---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, buildBreadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Terms of Service | PictoJXL';
const description =
  'Terms for using PictoJXL on pictojxl.com: acceptable use, IP ownership of your images, warranties, liability limits, and governing law.';

const jsonLd = [
  buildBreadcrumbLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms of Service', path: '/terms-of-service' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms-of-service" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <LegalPage
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="Ground rules for using the PictoJXL studio at pictojxl.com."
    updated="October 27, 2026"
  >
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) apply to <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>pictojxl.com</a> and the
      PictoJXL tools on it (together, the “Service”). The operator is
      <strong>Webwise Private Company Ltd</strong>, a United States company (“Webwise,” “we,” “us”).
      Access or use of the Service constitutes agreement to these Terms. If you disagree, leave the
      site unused.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What PictoJXL provides</h2>
    <p>
      PictoJXL is a client-side studio for inspecting and converting images to and from JPEG XL and
      related formats. Computation runs in your browser via WebAssembly and related APIs. We do not
      host a cloud conversion endpoint that accepts your image uploads for processing.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree that you will not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hammer the Service with bots, scrapers, or scripts meant to overload or disrupt it;</li>
      <li>Attempt denial-of-service activity or interfere with other visitors;</li>
      <li>Use the studio to handle illegal, abusive, or otherwise unlawful material;</li>
      <li>
        Convert or redistribute copyrighted works unless you own the rights or have permission;
      </li>
      <li>Probe, break, or misuse site infrastructure beyond ordinary use of the converter.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may suspend or block access when we reasonably believe these Terms were broken.</p>

    <h2>3. Who owns what</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Your pictures:</strong> You keep full ownership of images you process. Because
      conversion stays on your device and files are not uploaded to our conversion servers, Webwise
      does not claim ownership, license, or leftover rights in those images.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Our materials:</strong> Branding, interface, documentation, and software for the
      Service (other than your images and third-party components under their own licenses) belong to
      Webwise or its licensors and are protected by applicable IP law.
    </p>

    <h2>4. No warranties</h2>
    <p>
      THE SERVICE IS OFFERED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE,” WITHOUT EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY
      WARRANTIES, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND
      NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE FULLEST EXTENT LAW ALLOWS.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not promise perfect encodes, uninterrupted availability on every device, or output that
      matches every expectation. Very large or high-resolution files may exceed local browser or
      hardware limits and can slow, fail, or crash a tab. Keep your own backups of important files.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Liability cap</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WEBWISE AND ITS DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AND AFFILIATES
      ARE NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE
      DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, GOODWILL, OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITY, ARISING FROM
      USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICE—EVEN IF TOLD SUCH DAMAGES WERE POSSIBLE.
    </p>
    <p>
      Aggregate liability for claims tied to the Service will not exceed the greater of (a) amounts
      you paid us for the Service in the prior twelve (12) months, if any, or (b) zero U.S. dollars
      when the Service was free.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Ads and other third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Ads or third-party scripts (for example Google AdSense) may appear. Your dealings with those
      parties follow their terms and policies, not these Terms alone.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Privacy reference</h2>
    <p>
      How information is handled is described in the
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these Terms. The “Last updated” date will move when we publish changes. Keep
      using the Service after a change and you accept the revised Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by United States law and the law of the State where Webwise keeps its
      principal place of business, without conflict-of-law rules that would point elsewhere, except
      where mandatory consumer protections in your jurisdiction require otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Webwise Private Company Ltd<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
